{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quotient Ring.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quotient Ring.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quotient ring quotient ring","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quotient Ring.md","fileName":"Quotient Ring.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quotient Ring","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ring and Ideal Foundations]] · [[Quotient Rings and Ideals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Quotient Rings and Ideals","Ideal","Ring Homomorphism","Integral Domain","Field","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quotient Ring.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quotient Ring.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quotient ring quotient ring","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quotient Ring.md","fileName":"Quotient Ring.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quotient Ring","heading":"Quotient Ring","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Given an [[Ideal]] I in a ring R, the quotient ring R/I consists of additive cosets of I. Two elements represent the same coset when their difference lies in I, so every element of I becomes zero in the quotient.\n\nThe natural map R → R/I is a surjective [[Ring Homomorphism]] with kernel I. Quotients translate ideal properties into ring properties: prime ideals yield [[Integral Domain]] quotients and maximal ideals yield [[Field]] quotients.\n\nThe book first translates the additive coset rules from groups and then shows that an ideal permits multiplication by (a+I)(b+I)=ab+I. This gives the quotient both its ring operations and its natural projection map.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Quotient Rings and Ideals","Ideal","Ring Homomorphism","Integral Domain","Field","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quotient Ring.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quotient Ring.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quotient ring quotient ring","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quotient Ring.md","fileName":"Quotient Ring.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quotient Ring","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Quotient Rings and Ideals","Ideal","Ring Homomorphism","Integral Domain","Field","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}